'''Mog Adana''' was a [[human]] [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]]<ref name="Databank" /> of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="Teach / Corrupt" /> He<ref name="Databank" /> received a [[distress signal]] from [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]] from the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Khofar]]<ref name="Teach / Corrupt" /> in [[132 BBY]]<ref name="Date">{{TheAcolyteDate}}</ref> and informed Master [[Vernestra Rwoh]], for whom he did the desk work.<ref name="Teach/Corrupt Trivia">{{SW|url=teach-corrupt-trivia-gallery-the-acolyte|text="Teach / Corrupt" Trivia Gallery &#124; The Acolyte}}</ref> Rwoh prepared a team to head to [[Khofar]] to speak with Sol and investigate the murders of several Jedi. Adana was amongst those selected for the mission. They arrived at Khofar just after Sol's [[Polan GX-8]] jumped to [[hyperspace]]. Rwoh led her team through the jungles. They found the corpses of [[Jecki Lon]], [[Yord Fandar]], [[Ithia Paan]], and the other members of Sol's team. Adana informed Rwoh there was no sign of [[Verosha Aniseya]] or her twin [[Mae-ho Aniseya]], concluding they must have survived.<ref name="Teach / Corrupt" />

Rwoh asked Adana what he saw. He told her he saw an explosion, then a battle, one versus many. [[The Stranger|His]] power was extraordinary, his skills erratic, with the sole aim of leaving no survivors. After destroying an attacking [[umbramoth]] with her [[Vernestra Rwoh's purple-bladed lightsaber|lightwhip]], Rwoh told Adana that all the victims were killed by a lightsaber and asked him what that told him. Adana concluded a powerful Jedi had fallen. He asked if Rwoh thought Sol was the one responsible for the murders, to which Rwoh retorted that was quite the accusation. Adana asked if Sol caused the murders and why would he send a distress signal. Rwoh replied it was time to return to the ship and that they should prepare the bodies of the fallen Jedi for burial.<ref name="Teach / Corrupt" />

Some time later, Adana spoke with Rwoh inside the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]], informing her that [[Senator]] [[Worus Rayencourt]] had come to visit her. Rwoh became annoyed that Adana allowed the senator into the control room. Adana later informed Rwoh that they tracked down Sol on [[Brendok]] after Sol turned his transponder back on. She told him to prepare [[Cantaros|her starship]] for departure and to gather as many [[Jedi Knight]]s as he could without raising alarm. When Adana asked if she was anticipating a confrontation, she replied she was seeking to implement a resolution.<ref name="The Acolyte">{{Acolyte|The Acolyte (episode)}}</ref>

After the ''[[Cantaros]]'' arrived on Brendok, Rwoh sensed the presence of her former padawan as she exited the ship. Without revealing it to Adana or the rest of the Jedi, she told them to follow her into the [[Brendok fortress]]. Before Adana entered the fortress, [[Bazil]] rendezvoused with Adana, relieving the padawan. After they entered the fortress, Rwoh ordered two Jedi to search the premises, while Adana was sent to search the surrounding area outside the fortress with Bazil [[Tracker|tracking]] for their suspects. With the aid of Bazil's tracking, Adana eventually found an amnesic [[Mae-ho Aniseya|Mae Aniseya]] by a [[Bunta tree]]. He told her to not move, lay down any weapons she had and surrender. He then told Mae she was under arrest. The amnesic Mae was confused and asked him why she was being arrested.<ref name="The Acolyte" />

